      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Resplendent Temple [zone=811]\n**Who:**\n- Chancellor Corcelia [npc=38727]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Alaran Language:** | 73\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Experience\n- Money\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Large Sack of Waste [item=100099]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Reklor Irespine [npc=38732]\n- Surmo [npc=38742]\n- a Nitore butcher [npc=39742]\n- a decayed sentry stone [npc=38724]\n- a filthy swinetor [npc=38729]\n- a putrid swinetor [npc=38745]\n- a roaming swinetor [npc=38748]\n- a swinetor summoner [npc=38757]\n- a swinetor youth [npc=38760]\n- dead surmo [npc=38743]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Resplendent #1: The Light Within [quest=5466]\n- Resplendent #2: An Initiate's Task [quest=5467]\n- Secrets of the Stones [quest=5477]\n- Two Sides of the Stone [quest=5478]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 1\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 24 00:01:30 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This is the third in a series of three; a solo task that begins with Chancellor Corcelia in the Resplendent Temple, located at 1700, -15, -22 (inside the front door if coming in from Sarith)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"The Light Within\"\n\\- Completion of \"An Initiate's Task\"\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Chancellor Corcelia'\n_Without pre-requisites:_\nChancellor Corcelia completely ignores your presence.\n_With pre-requisites:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Chancellor Corcelia'\nChancellor Corcelia wrinkles alir nose in disgust as you step near. 'What is that foul [smell] that surrounds you?'\nYou say, 'Me? Smell?'\nChancellor Corcelia ignores your words as al steps closer. Without permission, the disgusted Nitore rifles through your bags, retrieving the offending items before placing them into a burlap sack. With alir hand extended far from alir body, al hands you a large pile of waste. 'Do not bring such filth before me! Did you not learn anything from our attendant? You must [dispose] of this refuse immediately!\nYou say, 'OK, I'll dispose of it...'\nChancellor Corcelia waves a hand at you dismissively, 'Return to Surmo at once and get rid of this waste.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'At Your Disposal'.\nAt Chancellor Corcelia's request, deliver the large sack of waste to Surmo so that he can dispose of it.\n\n---\n\nGive the Large Sack of Waste to Surmo 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_On hand-in:_\nSurmo looks at the size of the chute and then glances back at the sack of waste with a sigh, 'This bag is much too big. It will never fit!' With as much effort as he can muster, the halfling attempts to stuff the sack into the chute. Clearly not fitting, Surmo uses the weight of his body to shove the bag in, but when it finally budges, the clumsy halfling goes tumbling after!\nFind out what happened to Surmo 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ Surmo seems to have slipped down the trash chute.\n_Follow Surmo down the chute, clear the mobs in the area. You'll see large cauldrons and a scene that will leave Halflings of all types cringing. As you approach the dead Halflings, 2x \"a Nitore butcher\" spawn (hit for a max ~12,000; stunnable but not mezzable)._\n_NOTE: These butchers will despawn if you leave them idle for more than 60 seconds, but are reportedly re-triggerable._\nKill the Nitore butchers 0/2 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ You've been ambushed by Nitore butchers who appear to have harmed Surmo.\nReport your findings to Chancellor Corcelia 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\nYou say, 'Hail, Chancellor Corcelia'\nChancellor Corcelia glowers at you, clearly seething from your accusations, 'How dare you speak out against the Nitore! We welcomed you into our home, and this is how you repay us, by attempting to tarnish our good name? We are the chosen! The purest beings you will ever encounter. Guards! Remove this traitor from my sight!'\nFind a way out of the cell 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_You'll be ported to a jail cell, after which you'll see:_\na melodic voice flows into your ears from an unknown direction, 'Well isn't this a pity. How is it that someone like you ends up in the bowels of such a duplicitous temple? It appears as though you could use a little [help].'\n_Stand in the middle of the cell, visible, and with no target, and say \"help\" and \"seek\":_\nYou say, 'I need help!'\na melodic voice drifts through the air, 'I would love to help, really I would. But you see, I could use a little help myself. It's a bit lonely beneath the temple. No one visits, no one prays. I've been discarded, tossed aside. If I show you an exit, will you [seek] me out and complete one small and simple task?'\nYou say, 'I'll seek you out'\na melodic voice speaks only to you, 'Find me nestled beneath the temple amongst the st aming heaps of profuse filth.'\nYour task 'At Your Disposal' has been updated.\nFind the origin of the melodic voice 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ The voice that whispered to you said it could be found beneath the temple, in a place known as the in-between.\n_The origin is \"a decayed sentry stone\" in the far northeastern part of the \"In Between\"._\nYou say, 'Hail, a decayed sentry stone'\na decayed sentry stone is surrounded by a putrid aura which strengthens as you approach, 'It pleases me to see you've found your way here, to the true heart of the temple where imperfections are embraced. The Nitore are obsessed with their plight for purity, casting their unwanted waste into the bowels below, but they are limited in what they can attain. Perfection has its peak, you realize. Filth on the other hand, festers and swells, multiplying in both power and reach.' The decayed sentry stone pulses as the melodic voice continues, 'I assume your presence indicates that you are [ready] to complete your end of the bargain?'\nYou say, 'I'm ready'\na decayed sentry stone speaks in a voice only you can hear, 'There was a time when living amongst the grime was enough to satiate my hunger, warm waves of decay washing over my surroundings. Lately it's simply not enough. The beasts that roam these pits I call home are brimming with disease, their insides spoiled. I desire the blackened hearts of these pig-people. Fret not, no one will miss them, and their deaths will bring me much joy.'\nKill swinetor and retrieve their filthy hearts 0/4 (Resplendent Temple)\n_This updates randomly as you kill \"swinetor\" mobs (not an actual drop). Emote upon success:_\nYou rip a blackened heart from the chest of a swinetor corpse.\nReturn to the decayed sentry stone 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\nYou say, 'Hail, a decayed sentry stone'\na decayed sentry stone calls to you without using spoken words, 'You've done what I've asked; you've brought me the sickly hearts of many swinetor, but I fear the hunger has not been subdued. It gnaws at my essence, refusing to be ignored. I am but a prisoner to my desires. Please, I implore you; assist me with one last request. There is a Nitore found on the highest floor of the temple who has managed to escape corruption. Bring to alir untainted heart and I shall reward you with treasures beyond your wildest dreams.'\nSeek out a pure soul 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ The voice coming from the decayed stone has pleaded with you to recover a pure heart from the uncorrupted Nitore who dwells on the top floor of the temple.\n_Find Reklor Irespine all the way at the top of the temple, at about 1800, -100, 436 (travel up the middle parts of the temple)._\nYou say, 'Hail, Reklor Irespine'\nReklor Irespine appears rather annoyed at your presence, 'Can you not see I am busy with my [research]? What is it that you [want]?'\nYou say, 'I want information!'\nReklor Irespine eyes you cautiously before speaking, 'An air of disease surrounds you, outsider. I hope you have not given in to the corruption that lives within this temple, like so many others. I have [knowledge] to share with those who will listen, but anything else you may want from me will not be taken without a [fight].'\nYou say, 'What about your research and knowledge?'\nReklor Irespine looks you over with cautious eyes before responding, 'I've been investigating the curious dichotomy of the sentry stones found within the temple. The Nitore reveal in beauty, praying to their immaculate sentry stones, and the pig-people below worship their ruined remains. Both relics appear to be cut from the same stone, yet the two represent two very different ideals. Have you ever heard these stones speak?'\nYou say, 'Yes, I've heard them speak'\nReklor Irespine nods with enthusiasm, 'And doesn't their voice sometimes sound strikingly similar? It is my belief these stones are one in the same; two sides of a very twisted being. I am glad I have found a confidant in you, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_. Hopefully we can work together to get to the bottom of this mystery.'\nYou have uncovered the horrible connection between the temple and the in-between below.\n_Note that if you say \"fight\" to Reklor Irespine, he attacks (hits for a max ~65,000)._\n_Rewards:_\nExperience\n410 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Priceless Beauty\n- Eltarki's Diary - Priceless Beauty [item=99799]",
