      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Resplendent Temple [zone=811]\n**Who:**\n- Reklor Irespine [npc=38732]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 95\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Decayed Stone Fragment [item=100572]\n- Radiant Stone Fragment [item=100622]\n- Reconstructed Sentry Stone [item=100656]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Resplendent Temple: Secrets of the Stones [zone=829]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Reklor Irespine [npc=39190]\n- a decayed sentry stone [npc=39188]\n- a radiant sentry stone [npc=39189]\n- a reconstructed sentry stone [npc=40583]\n- an ornate chest - Secrets of the Stones [npc=39191]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Resplendent #1: The Light Within [quest=5466]\n- Resplendent #2: An Initiate's Task [quest=5467]\n- Resplendent #3: At Your Disposal [quest=5468]\n- Two Sides of the Stone [quest=5478]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 24 00:07:37 2011\nModified: Sat Feb 8 15:50:13 2020 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n\n---\n\n_This group mission begins with Reklor Irespine in the Resplendent Temple, located at 1810, -100, 440 (from the Pillars zone-in, head due south into the building and continue south until you come to the last room; Reklor is in the southeast room)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"The Light Within\"\n\\- Completion of \"An Initiate's Task\"\n\\- Completion of \"At Your Disposal\"\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Reklor Irespine'\n_Without pre-requisites:_\nReklor Irespine appears more interested in reading than speaking to you.\n_With pre-requisites:_\nYou say, 'Hail, Reklor Irespine'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'Since my [revelation], I have devoted every waking minute to uncovering the truth surrounding the sentry stones. The Nitore will have you believe that the stones they prominently display are the only stones in existence, yet you and I both know that not to be true. I believe that the Nitore have [hidden] away many more stones, possibly to stifle the voices that speak of things other than beauty.'\nYou say, 'What about your revelation?'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'Do you really wish to hear my history? It will surprise you, I'm sure. While my [story] doesn't directly involve the task at hand, I suppose it could shed some light on why I'm still here.'\nYou say, 'What's your story?'\nReklor Irespine speaks with a reminiscent smile, 'It has been quite some time since I left my studies in Sarith to follow my kin and alir dream of finding peace and purity at the edge of the temple. While I'd originally thought I'd find myself bored and uninspired, I instead found a mentor in Chancellor Corcelia, who insisted she saw a light within me. Before too long I, myself, became a mindful [member] of the Nitore, praising purity and shunning anything that didn't shine in the resplendent light that Ladrys had bestowed upon us.'\nYou say, 'You were a member?'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'Over time I abandoned my cerebral studies, instead focusing my full attention on how to [rid] myself of decay and achieve the highest form of beauty. Still a mortal being at my core, my body inched closer to death every day. This was not suitable for someone so obsessed with perfection. I was not alone in my ideals, however.'\nYou say, 'How did you rid yourself of it?'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'Long before the first stones were placed to erect this temple, the Nitore had devised a way to separate the purity and [waste] within one's soul. The former consumed by the cleansed to feed their insatiable hunger for perfestion, and the latter, discreetly disposed of and left to fester.'\nYou say, 'Waste?'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'Many would believe this temple was constructed to house the splendor that the Nitore claim to hold in such high regard, but the truth is something much more sinister. The beautiful walls designed to retain resplendence, were in fact built to cover up the pit of waste that grew along with the Nitore's aesthetic [greed].'\nYou say, 'Greed?'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'Without much interest in anything other than perfection, I spent my days praying to the sentry stones, hoping they would sing songs of beauty in my presence. For days and days I sat, surrounded by nothing but silence. After nearly a week without moving, I finally heard a faint whisper from within the sentry stone, yet it was nothing like I had expected. The soft, sweet song I had hoped to hear instead manifested in a guttural tone that gnawed at my ears. The [voice] hissed of disease and decay, beckoning me to venture beneath the temple and bask in filth.'\nYou say, 'What voice?'\nReklor Irespine shakes alir head at the memory still fresh in alir mind, 'I thought I must be going crazy. How could these relics of beauty praise such imperfection? That haunting question was enough to ignite the spark of curiosity within me once again, and from that day forth I spent my time buried in research, determined to uncover the truth surrounding the sentry stones.'\nYou say, 'Where have the Nitore hidden more stones?'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'You have already found a stone beneath the temple that I hadn't discovered. Why couldn't there be more? I'd say the stone's desire for my death is a clear indication that my research is headed in the right direction. Will you [help] me, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_?'\nYou say, 'I'll help'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'I am very grateful. It is a lonely eyistence, living as a shrouded outsider amidst the Nitore. My purity has already been called into question. I fear what would become of me if I were caught searching the in-between for stones that aren't supposed to exist. You on the other hand, could travel into the [depths] of the temple almost unnoticed.'\nYou say, 'The depths?'\nReklor Irespine nods, 'The in-between is where I believe our search should start. Let me know when you are ready to [begin], and I hill see that you get there safely.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Secrets of the Stones'.\nReklor Irespine has asked that you locate and destroy any sentry stones found within the temple, collecting any stone fragments in the process.\nYou say, 'Ready to begin!'\nReklor Irespine leads you to the in-between beneath the temple.\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Resplendent Temple.\n\n---\n\nLocate and destroy sentry stones beneath the temple 0/3 (Resplendent Temple)\nLoot Decayed Stone Fragments from the sentry stones 0/3 (Resplendent Temple)\nLocate and destroy sentry stones within the temple 0/3 (Resplendent Temple)\nLoot Radiant Stone Fragments from the sentry stones 0/3 (Resplendent Temple)\n_The Sentry Stones' spawn locations may be random. They tend to appear in small side rooms in the \"In Between\" (for the decay stones) and the second floor of the temple (for the radiants)._\n_The stones hit for a max ~12,000 and cast \"Drifting Decay\" or \"Surge of Radiance\":_\nDrifting Decay: PB AE 50', Disease (-900)\n1: Decrease Movement by 80%\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 18200 per tick\nSurge of Radiance: PB AE 200', Magic (-900)\n1: Unknown #343\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 26700\nDeliver the Decayed Stone Fragments to Reklor Irespine 0/3 (Resplendent Temple)\nDeliver the Radiant Stone Fragments to Reklor Irespine 0/3 (Resplendent Temple)\nSpeak to Reklor Irespine 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\nYou say, 'Hail, Reklor Irespine'\nReklor Irespine takes special care when handling the stone fragments, gently turning each piece until it locks firmly with another. A rush of whispers roll through the air as the focused Alaran reassembles the fragments to form something new. With a bit of reluctance and an unsteady hand, Reklor gives you the [reconstructed] stones.\n_You receive 5x \"Reconstructed Sentry Stone\"._\nYou say, 'What about these reconstructed stones?'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'Place one of these stones in each of the alcoves surrounding this room. If my research is correct, we should be able to summon whatever it is that speaks through these stones.'\nPlace the reconstructed sentry stones in the alcoves around the room 0/5 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Right-click the stones in each of the five small alcoves around the room. As you do the last one, be ready for a fight._\n_NOTE: The task locks here._\nKeep an eye on Reklor Irespine in case something goes wrong... 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ Unsure what power the reconstructed stones may have, Reklor has asked that you keep an eye on ali.\nReklor Irespine is possessed by an unseen force.\nSubdue Reklor Irespine while al is possessed 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Reklor Irespine hits for a max ~15,000 and casts both \"Drifting Decay\" and \"Surge of Radiance\". Fight him to about 25% health at which point he'll go inactive._\n_**NOTE: Don't DPS it too hard or you could wind up killing him. If he dies before the task updates, hail his corpse to get the update.**_\nSpeak with Reklor Irespine 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ The visibly weakened Reklor Irespine beckons you to ali.\nYou say, 'Hail, Reklor Irespine'\nReklor Irespine uses what little strength al has to stand and face you, a wave of regret washing over alir face, 'What have I done? Please tell me you aren't hurt! I could never forgive myself...' The distraught Alaran motions slowly to the back room, 'You'll find a trunk that contains my most valued possessions in the room to the south west. Please, take whatever you wish. It is the only way I will absolve this guilt over what I have done.'\nClaim your reward from the ornate chest 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n_Task Window Says:_ Reklor Irespine has offered you a reward for your invaluable help.\nWhile assisting Reklor Irespine in alir research, you managed to discover many sentry stones within the Resplendent Temple that hold unusual power.\nYou say, 'Hail, Reklor Irespine'\nReklor Irespine speaks with a sense of urgency, 'I suggest we [leave] at once, before whatever possessed me returns.'\nYou say, 'I wish to leave'\nLOADING, PLEASE WAIT...\nYou have entered The Resplendent Temple.\n_Rewards:_\n341 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Priceless Beauty\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item + 1 Cantrip per Task)\nA King's Ransom\nAmber of the Culicidae\nBejeweled Loop of the Ambassador\nEnergetic Rod\nLuminous Monocle of the Scribe\nScar of Rex\nSlorn's Ceremonial Drape\nSpiked Pauldrons of the Prismatic Selyrah\nTri-Shield of the King\nWarmace of the High Guard\nGreater Alarin Cantrip\nMedian Alaran Cantrip\n\n---\n- Eltarki's Diary - Priceless Beauty [item=99799]\n- Median Alaran Cantrip [item=98717]",
