      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Resplendent Temple [zone=811]\n**Who:**\n- Reklor Irespine [npc=38732]\nRating:\n0/0**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Task\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Time Limit:** | 06:00:00\n**Success Lockout Timer**: 06:00:00\n**Quest Items:**\n- Book of Chants [item=60920]\n- Book of Prayers [item=60919]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Resplendent Temple: Two Sides of the Stone [zone=830]\n**Related Creatures:**\n- Avatar of Ladrys [npc=39193]\n- Avatar of Sholoth [npc=39194]\n- Purity Stone [npc=39873]\n- Shadow of Decay [npc=39195]\n- Vision of Splendor [npc=39196]\n- a decayed sentry stone [npc=39871]\n- a diseased stone [npc=39870]\n- a mirror image [npc=39874]\n- a perfect stone [npc=39869]\n- a pool of waste [npc=39875]\n- a sentry stone [npc=39868]\n- a splendorous sentry stone [npc=39872]\n- an ornate chest - Two Sides of the Stone [npc=39192]\n- inner darkness [npc=39197]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Resplendent #1: The Light Within [quest=5466]\n- Resplendent #2: An Initiate's Task [quest=5467]\n- Resplendent #3: At Your Disposal [quest=5468]\n- Secrets of the Stones [quest=5477]\n**Era:** | !Veil of Alaris\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Group\n**Min. # of Players:** | 3\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 24 00:51:08 2011\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Veil of Alaris Information & Guides: An Overview \\| Group Progression & Task List \\| Raid Progression \\| Visible Armor**\n**NOTE: This is the quest entry for the group version of \"Two Sides of the Stone\". See this quest entry [quest=5541] for the raid version.**\n\n---\n\n_This group mission begins with Reklor Irespine in the Resplendent Temple, located at 1810, -100, 440 (from the Pillars zone-in, head due south into the building and continue south until you come to the last room; Reklor is in the southeast room)._\n_Pre-requisites for requesting the task:_\n\\- Completion of \"The Light Within\"\n\\- Completion of \"An Initiate's Task\"\n\\- Completion of \"At Your Disposal\"\n\\- Completion of \"Secrets of the Stones\"\n\\- 73 Skill Level in Alaran\n\n---\n\nYou say, 'Hail, Reklor Irespine'\n_Without pre-requisites:_\nReklor Irespine appears more interested in reading than speaking to you.\n_With pre-requisites:_\nReklor Irespine reaches out for you as al struggles to speak, 'I owe you my life, \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_, and many apologies. My mind and body betrayed me as a foreign [essence] entered my soul, bringing with it a volatile rage which I was unable to control. Without your [help], I fear the possessing spirit would have taken over completely.'\nYou say, 'What essence?'\nReklor Irespine winces as al recalls the recent events, 'As you placed the stones within the temple, I felt a surge of energy flow through the air. It was as though the sentry stones were conduits for spirits of some sort, allowing passage from their world into this one. Once the final stone was set, a crippling wave rushed over me. My body was still, but I could feel my veins begin to flow with a foreign power... And then I blacked out, only to awake [broken] and filled with painful regret over what I had unknowingly done.'\nYou say, 'Broken?'\nReklor Irespine pauses, sucking in air with visible discomfort, 'I fear I won't ever fully recover from the trauma my body received, but something must be done. The power within the force that possessed me; it was greater than anything I have ever known. Where a [power] like that could come from? I can hardly guess, but it seems to manifest itself using the sentry stones.'\nYou say, 'What about the power?'\nReklor Irespine speaks with certainty, 'It is clear to me what needs to be done. The sentry stones must be destroyed. I am no match for the power they contain, but you somehow managed to resist possession. Whether by luck or mental fortitude, it does not matter. Tell me, do you have a large force [willing] to destroy the stones, or perhaps you are [able] to complete the task with a smaller group?'\nYou say, 'We're able to do so with a small group'\nReklor Irespine says, in Alaran, 'Maintain your focus, and keep our goal at the forefront of your mind. Let me know when you are [prepared] to begin.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Two Sides of the Stone'.\nYou say, 'We're prepared!'\nReklor Irespine bows deeply with gratitude, 'I will pray for your success.'\n\n---\n\n**Summary**\n\\- Don't zone out, the event will reset and you will have to start all over again.\n\\- Hail the sentry stone to spawn the Avatar\n\\- Take the Avatar down to 75%\n\\- Decay #1\n\\-\\-\\- Use no cures here; stay in zombie form and keep the DOTs on you.\n\\- Splendor #1\n\\-\\-\\- One person must click off all their buffs (including songs and auras), and stay buffless.\n\\- Take the Avatar down to 50%\n\\- Decay #2\n\\-\\-\\- The named will emote for someone to jump out the window.\n\\- Splendor #2\n\\-\\-\\- Everyone must cure \"Filth\" by running to the location of the \"Purity Stone\".\n\\- Take the Avatar down to 25%\n\\- Decay #3\n\\-\\-\\- Keep a book passed around.\n\\- Splendor #3\n\\-\\-\\- Keep a book passed around.\n\\- Kill the Avatar\n\n---\n\n03. Speak to the sentry stone 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\n_NOTE: Don't hail the sentry stone until you're ready for a fight._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, a sentry stone'\n\n\n\n\na sentry stone begins to tremble as whispers of beauty and decay fill the room.\n\n\n\n\n_The Avatar of Ladrys spawns and attacks._\n\n04. Engage the avatar spawned by the stone 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\n_It hits for a max ~12,500 and shifts forms between \"Avatar of Ladrys\" and \"Avatar of Sholoth\". Ladrys casts \"Purification\" while Sholoth casts \"Wave of Filth\":_\n\n\n\nPurification: Single Target, Disease (-900)\n\n\n1: 60% Chance to trigger: Ruin Magic _(a dispell)_\n\n2: Silence _(1 tick)_\n\n\n\nWave of Filth: Single Target, Disease (-900)\n\n\n1: Amnesia (Silence vs Melee Effect) _(1 tick)_\n\n2: Decrease HP when cast by 27700\n\n\n\n\n_While the Avatar is in Ladrys' form, adds called \"inner darkness\" spawn. These take the form of a player and attack, hitting for a max ~9,000. They have an emote:_\n\n\n\nThe inner darkness is becoming very unstable.\n\n\n\n\n_Shortly after that emote, they explode (despawn), casting the AE \"Inner Darkness\" in the process:_\n\n\n\nInner Darkness: PB AE 30', Magic (-900)\n\n\n1: Blindness (1)\n\n\n2: Decrease HP when cast by 43300\n\n\n\n\n_While the Avatar is in Sholoth's form, untargetable black oozes spawn on random people. These have a damage aura, so step away from them (they despawn after a short time):_\n\n\n\nSludge: Single Target 0', Disease (-900)\n\n\n1: Decrease Movement by 60%\n\n\n2: Decrease Mana by 5000\n\n\n3: Decrease Endurance by 2000\n\n\n4: Decrease Hitpoints by 26300\n\n\n\n\n_Once the Avatar reaches 75%, it goes inactive. You see:_\n\n\n\nAvatar of Ladrys trembles while crashing to the floor as the essences of decay and splendor flee, causing the sentry stone to split in two.\n\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ The possessing essence has split, fleeing to the west and east towers. Hail the sentry stones to travel to the towers and defeat the beings that now dwell there.\n\n\n\n\n_This opens up the next two steps and spawns two stones at either side of the room: \"a perfect stone\" and \"a diseased stone\". You'll find one named in each of the temple's two towers: The Shadow of Decay and the Vision of Splendor. To get to these mobs, you use these two stones._\n\n\n\n_When ready, either walk into the stone's proximity (you'll automatically port to their tower), or follow their dialogue:_\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, a diseased stone'\n\n\n\n\na diseased stone emits faint whispers of [decay].\n\n\n\n\n_Walking into the stone or saying \"decay\" ports up to the Shadow of Decay's tower._\n\n\n\nYou say, 'Hail, a perfect stone'\n\n\n\n\na perfect stone emits faint whispers of [splendor].\n\n\n\n\n_Walking into the stone or saying \"splendor\" ports up to the Vision of Splendor's tower._\n\n\n\n_NOTE: You can do either tower first; it doesn't matter. You can also take a break before porting up to a tower. There is no timer (other than the task timer itself)._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n05. Defeat the Shadow of Decay 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\nThe Shadow of Decay calls to all those before it, 'I demand an offering of rot and decay, made from the flesh of your own!'\n\n\n\n\nAll must succumb to rot in order to make an offer of flesh.\n\n\n\n\n_The Shadow of Decay hits for a max ~12,500 and AEs \"Rot\", which leads to \"Decaying Flesh\" (which gives a zombie illusion):_\n\n\n\nRot: Targeted AE 30', Disease (-900)\n\n\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 14000 per tick\n\n\n2: Increase corruption counter by 30\n\n\n3: Improved Spell Effect: Decaying Flesh\n\n\n\n\nDecaying Flesh: Self 0', Corruption (-900)\n\n\n1: 100% Chance to trigger: Zombie Rot\n\n\n2: Decrease Hitpoints by 8400 per tick\n\n\n3: Increase corruption counter by 30\n\n\n4: Decrease Attack Speed by 40%\n\n\n\n\n_Don't use any cures or anything that has a cure component. The DOTs and illusion must stay on everyone in order to keep the Shadow from regenerating. He'll check for this requirement every 6 seconds, so it must be kept on you at all times._\n\n\n\n_As long as even one person doesn't have the DOT/illusion on them, the Shadow will regenerate 25% per tick._\n\n\n\n_This step updates once you kill the Shadow._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n06. Defeat the Vision of Splendor 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\nVision of Splendor calls to all those before it, 'Impure souls, tainted with magic, are no challenge for me!'\n\n\n\n\nOne among many must rid themselves of all and any magical effects.\n\n\n\n\n_The Vision of Splendor hits for a max ~12,500 and casts the single-target one-tick duration \"Purification\" on random people:_\n\n\n\nPurification: Single Target, Disease (-900)\n\n\n1: 60% Chance to trigger: Ruin Magic _(a dispell)_\n\n2: Silence _(1 tick)_\n\n\n\n_Once the Vision emotes, one person needs to click off all their buffs and remain that way until it's dead. Note: Auras and songs count as well._\n\n\n\n_As long as everyone remains buffed, the Vision regenerates 25% per tick. Only one person needs to go buffless for this fight._\n\n\n\n_This step updates once you kill the Vision._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n07. Return to the central tower and engage the avatar once again 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ The essence is one, once again. Fight it within the central tower.\n\n\n\n\n_Don't port back down until you're ready for a fight. The Avatar switches forms and has the same fight abilities as earlier. Once it reaches 50%, it goes inactive and the next two steps open up._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n08. Defeat the Shadow of Decay 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\nOne among you must throw themselves from the tower as a sacrifice to Sholoth!\n\n\n\n\n_During this encounter, the Shadow of Decay casts \"Wave of Filth\":_\n\n\n\nWave of Filth: Single Target, Disease (-900)\n\n\n1: Amnesia (Silence vs Melee Effect) _(1 tick)_\n\n2: Decrease HP when cast by 27700\n\n\n\n\n_As the fight goes on, a random person (other than the tank) will get an emote. That person must jump out a window. (Note: Levitation effects greatly slow your jump speed, so click them off before initiating this portion of the event.)_\n\n\n\n_Everyone Sees:_ One among you must throw yourselves from the tower as a sacrifice to Sholoth!\n\n\n\n\n_Target Sees:_ Jump from this tower as the ultimate sacrifice to Sholoth!\n\n\n\n\n_On a Successful Jump:_ You have made the proper sacrifice.\n\n\n\n\n_On a Failed Jump (Shadow regens 25%):_ Shadow of Decay shouts, '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ failed to make the sacrifice!'\n\n\n\n\n_NOTE: Only the player with the emote should make the jump. If you have the emote and jump, you'll be ported back into the room. If you don't have the emote, you'll simply fall to your death._\n\n\n\n_This step updates once you kill the Shadow._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n09. Defeat the Vision of Splendor 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\nVision of Splendor calls to those within its reach, 'Cleanse yourself of the filth that surrounds you!'\n\n\n\n\n_The Vision still casts the \"Purification\" spell on random targets:_\n\n\n\nPurification: Single Target, Disease (-900)\n\n\n1: 60% Chance to trigger: Ruin Magic _(a dispell)_\n\n2: Silence _(1 tick)_\n\n\n\n_In addition, it will cast the spell \"Filth\" on everyone but its target (the tank):_\n\n\n\nFilth: Single Target, Unresistable (-900)\n\n\n1: Decrease Hitpoints by 27000 per tick\n\n\n\n\n_At the same time this happens, a \"Purity Stone\" (sentry stone model appears at a random spot around the room's perimeter). You have about six seconds to move to its location to cure the \"Filth\" spell. You'll see this emote when the Vision AEs \"Filth\":_\n\n\n\nYou must cleanse yourself near the purity stone.\n\n\n\n\n_You'll see this once you've been cleaned:_\n\n\n\nYou have been cleansed.\n\n\n\n\n_If someone fails, you'll see this (and the Vision regenerates 25%):_\n\n\n\nVision of Splendor shouts '\\_\\_\\_\\_\\_ is still covered in filth!'\n\n\n\n\n_This step updates once you kill the Vision._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n10. Return to the central tower and engage the avatar once again 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\n_Don't port back down until you're ready for a fight. The Avatar switches forms and has the same fight abilities as earlier. Once it reaches 25%, it goes inactive and the next two steps open up._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n11. Defeat the Shadow of Decay 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\nShadow of Decay calls to all within its reach, 'Sing your chants of decay! Fill your minds and bodies with disease, or suffer my wrath!'\n\n\n\n\n_During this fight, black oozes spawn on random people. These have a damage aura (the same ones that spawn with the Avatar of Sholoth). The Shadow of Decay, itself, doesn't have any AEs here._\n\n\n\n_Shortly after engaging, a random person will be given a book, \"Book of Chants\" (you'll see an emote indicating who receives it)._\n\n\n\n_Keep the book passed around (target a player and right-click, do not trade the book). The book, when clicked, casts \"Chant of Decay\" on you. Everyone has to keep this spell up via the book:_\n\n\n\nChant of Decay: Single 0', Unresistable (-900)\n\n\n1: Amnesia (Silence vs Melee Effect) _(2 ticks)_\n\n2: Decrease Endurance by 300 per tick\n\n\n3: Decrease Hitpoints by 11300 per tick\n\n\n4: Trigger Effect: Strained Voice on Fade\n\n\n\n\n_NOTE: If \"Chant of Decay\" fades from you, a new effect takes over: \"Strained Voice\" (lasts 1-2 ticks and still counts toward the NPC's \"chant\" requirement)._\n\n\n_You can still click it, but you won't get rebuffed with \"Chant of Decay\" (which you need on you in order to prevent the NPC from regenerating)._\n\n\n\n\\\\* If you pass while you have Chant/Prayer, nothing bad happens, but the duration of Chant/Prayer does \\*not\\* update.\n\n\n\\\\* If you pass while you have Strained Voice, the mob heals.\n\n\n\n\nWhat you want to do then, is wait until \\*BOTH\\* have faded and then pass the book. This will start the effects all over again.\n\n\n\n\n_If you get \"Strained Voice\" on you, wait until it fades and then quickly pass the book along before the named takes notice._\n\n\n\n_Upon Passing the Book:_ You recite the Chant of Decay as you pass the book to \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\n\n\n\n\n_Upon Failure (Shadow regens 25%):_ The Chant of Decay must be maintained.\n\n\n\n\n_This step updates once you kill the Shadow._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n12. Defeat the Vision of Splendor 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\nVision of Splendor calls to all within its reach, 'Pray for purity, to cleanse your minds and bodies, or suffer my wrath!'\n\n\n\n\n_During this fight, \"inner darkness\" adds spawn and attack, hitting for a max ~9,000 and casting \"Inner Darkness\" (the same add types that spawn with the Avatar of Ladrys). The Vision of Splendor, itself, doesn't have any AEs here._\n\n\n\n_Shortly after engaging, a random person will be given a book, \"Book of Prayers\" (you'll see an emote indicating who receives it)._\n\n\n\n_Keep the book passed around (target a player and right-click). The book, when clicked, casts \"Prayer of Purity\" on you. Everyone has to keep this spell up via the book:_\n\n\n\nPrayer of Purity: Single 0', Unresistable (-900)\n\n\n1: Silence _(2 ticks)_\n\n2: Decrease Mana by 900 per tick\n\n\n3: Decrease Hitpoints by 11300 per tick\n\n\n4: Trigger Effect: Strained Voice on Fade\n\n\n\n\n_NOTE: If \"Prayer of Purity\" fades from you, a new effect takes over: \"Strained Voice\" (lasts 1-2 ticks and still counts toward the NPC's \"prayer\" requirement). This effect may impact your ability to click the book. You can pass it, but you won't get rebuffed with \"Prayer of Purity\" (which you need on you in order to prevent the NPC from regenerating)._\n\n\n\n_If you get \"Strained Voice\" on you, wait until it fades and then quickly pass the book along before the named takes notice._\n\n\n\n_Upon Passing the Book:_ You recite the Prayer of Purity as you pass the book to \\_\\_\\_\\_\\_.\n\n\n\n\n_Upon Failure (Vision regens 25%):_ The Prayer of Purity must be maintained.\n\n\n\n\n_This step updates once you kill the Vision._\n\n\n\n_NOTE: The task locks at this point._\n\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n\n13. Return to the central tower and defeat the avatar 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\n_Task Window Says:_ Defeat the possessed Nitore once and for all!\n\n\n\n\n_Don't port back down until you're ready for a fight. The Avatar switches forms and has the same fight abilities as earlier. This step updates upon its death._\n\n\n\nClaim your reward from the ornate chest 0/1 (Resplendent Temple)\n\n\n\n_Upon opening the chest:_\n\n\n\nYou have destroyed the corrupted sentry stones, so power can no longer flow through them within the Resplendent Temple.\n\n_Rewards:_\n273 platinum\nEltarki's Diary - Priceless Beauty\nPossible Chest Loot (1 Item per Task)\nBloody Scythe\nCollar of the Maw Lurker\nDingy Loop of the Slothlord\nGraven Ring of Grimlop\nKeystone Garnet\nPutrefied Earring of the Rat Queen\nSavage Boneblade\nSelyrah Skin Bag\nMedian Alaran Cantrip\nGreater Alaran Cantrip\n- Bloody Scythe [item=101024]\n- Collar of the Maw Lurker [item=100728]\n- Dingy Loop of the Slothlord [item=101043]\n- Eltarki's Diary - Priceless Beauty [item=99799]\n- Graven Ring of Grimlop [item=101155]\n- Greater Alaran Cantrip [item=99412]\n- Keystone Garnet [item=101446]\n- Median Alaran Cantrip [item=98717]\n- Putrefied Earring of the Rat Queen [item=101345]\n- Savage Boneblade [item=99874]\n- Selyrah Skin Bag [item=100915]",
    },
  },
}
